{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent low bias: forecasts are systematically below realized prices, especially during sustained uptrends. Apply an upward level shift (additive bias correction) that increases with horizon.",
    "Trend/lag error: the model reacts too slowly to regime changes (misses the post-dip rally). Use a momentum/trend filter—if the last 5–10 days show rising prices, tilt the entire path upward and steepen the slope.",
    "Horizon-dependent underestimation: error grows with lead time (small near days 1–3, large by days 10–30). Apply a horizon ramp correction (e.g., +x at day 1 rising to +y by day 30).",
    "Underpricing volatility/upside tails: the model compresses the distribution and misses higher highs. Increase forecast variance in bullish regimes (widen upside, lift peaks) rather than forcing mean reversion.",
    "Mean-reversion miscalibration: after a local drop, the model expects continued weakness/flatness while reality mean-reverts upward strongly. When recent drawdown is large but fundamentals/trend are positive, override mean reversion with a rebound term."
  ]
}
